      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A case is described of a 69-year-old man with angina pectoris who was found at coronary angiography to have all three coronary arteries arising by separate orifices from the right coronary sinus. This appears to be a previously unreported anomaly. The embryological origin and mechanisms of angina in coronary arterial anomalies are discussed."},
